275 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 85 0 R
/E (The project demonstrates concurrent TCP examination sessions, question delivery, answer submission, timer handling and score calculation. The two-client tests confirm that separate student sessions can be handled. The SDN controller performs MAC learning, packet forwarding and periodic flow-statistics collection. The iperf3 runs recorded lower throughput under the reduced-bandwidth condition. The link test showed that connectivity can be restored after a manual link recovery.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
276 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 85 0 R
/T (LIMITATIONS AND FUTURE WORK)
/E (LIMITATIONS AND FUTURE WORK)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
277 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 85 0 R
/E (The throughput figures are individual runs, not repeated averages. Application response time and fairness were not measured quantitatively. The controller does not yet perform congestion-based prioritisation or automatic rerouting. Future work can add dynamic traffic policies, automatic recovery, more simultaneous clients and repeated performance experiments.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
278 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 85 0 R
/T (CONCLUSION)
/E (CONCLUSION)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
279 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 85 0 R
/E (The project integrates a multi-client TCP examination application with an SDN-controlled Mininet network. It demonstrates reliable application communication, programmable packet forwarding and basic network monitoring in a controlled test environment.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
